# Without this file, `COPY . .` bakes the developer's .env into the production
# image. Because the entrypoint calls dotenv.config(), every variable Lightsail
# does NOT set is then silently filled in from that baked file — which is how
# production ended up making Stripe calls with a TEST key while the container
# environment carried a live one.
#
# Keep .env* first and never relax it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

.git
.gitignore
.github

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Local-only tooling and notes; none of it runs in the container.
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.md
!README.md
coverage
.nyc_output
tmp
